  {
    "title": "Where to draw the line",
    "body": "**Hybrid fan-out** pushes for ordinary accounts and pulls for large ones. The line comes from N1: a post must reach every follower within 10 seconds, at 100,000 writes per second, so pushing works up to 10 × 100,000 = **1,000,000 followers**. That is the threshold T. Accounts above it are not pushed: their recent posts sit in the large-posts cache, and followers read them when opening the feed. To avoid switching back and forth, an account moves to pull above 1,000,000 and back to push only below 800,000.",
