  {
    "title": "Failures and summary",
    "body": "**Fan-out backlog:** if workers fall behind, posts wait in the queue and feeds are older, but reading still works; alert when the oldest queued post is close to the 10-second target. **A cache node fails:** its replica takes over (N3); if both copies are lost, affected feeds are rebuilt by pulling from the posts store at each user's next open. **Summary:** F1 and F2 by the post and feed services; N1 by pushing only below 1,000,000 followers, at most 10 seconds per post; N2 by one cached feed plus a few large accounts, read in parallel; N3 by cache replicas and rebuilding by pull.",
